  "summary": "Flight 11 was the final Block 2 flight and the last launch from the original OLP-1 before its rebuild. The reflown Booster 15 tested landing burn configurations planned for Block 3 and was expended in the Gulf of Mexico, with 9 of 10 engines relighting for boostback. Ship 38 deployed eight Starlink simulators, relit a Raptor in space, tested heat shield tile changes, and made a controlled splashdown northwest of Australia at T+1:06:25.",
